		{"id":"n186","type":"text","x":0,"y":4526,"width":932,"height":150,"text":"⚠ DATA-QUALITY FLAGS (PI to confirm — not auto-corrected):\n• lamotrigine Adolescents 12-16 years: min_maintenance_dose (Z)=150 mg/day but helper min_maintenance (O)=100 mg/day; stray value 'P' in cell AI18.\n• lamotrigine >16 years: min_maintenance_dose (Z)=200 mg/day but helper min_maintenance (O)=150 mg/day (appears off by one increment).\n• oxcarbazepine >=70 kg: high_increments repeat 1900/2000/2100 mg/day - doses already reached in up_increments (AE=2000, AF=2100); likely copy error.\n• carbamazepine Adolescents 13-18 years: stray text 'to' in cell AC9 within the increment ladder.\n• carbamazepine Adults >18 years: helper columns internally inconsistent (divide-by=16 implies 75 mg step but ladder steps 100 mg; percent-cap 60% implies effective range 720 but N=960). Ladder itself climbs correctly 800->2000.\n• brivaracetam 11-<20 / 20-<50 / >=50 kg: range/effective-range helper columns have rounding/internal mismatches; actual ladders still reach the true max.","color":"3"},
